row('DEFER_SETUP','native/yuv-backend.c:29-39;web/yuv-presenter.js:41-43','Current crop occurs at presentation after full decoded planes. MPEG-2 region-limited reconstruction needs backward motion/interpolation/filter closure across pictures; changing viewport alone cannot implement the proposal.','Requested crop is exact to full MPEG-2 I/P decode with all transitive motion/filter support retained.','Trace one constrained crop dependency region and compare full-decode pixels; measure whether closure expands to most of the picture before editing decoder.','Out-of-crop predictor or filter-halo omission rejects, even if central pixels match.','Closed reconstructed area plus dependency analysis versus full picture decode.')
row('STOP_PROFILE','native/adaptation/flac.h:28-38;src/internal/playback-plans.ts:80-93','The selected Native adaptation explicitly preserves channel layout and does not admit an output downmix. Spectral mixing before synthesis requires that requested matrix plus compatible codec window/state; no such operation is available to optimize in this route.','Only an explicitly requested downmix may reorder compatible spectral synthesis while preserving overlap and numeric contract.','Reopen for one existing downmix decoder path and audit its AC3 optimized ordering before proposing a new transform change.','Per-channel nonlinear processing or different windows must prevent commutation.','Actual synthesis work after accounting for existing downmix optimization and mixing overhead.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','native/vd_browser.c:199-210;native/simd/h264-qpel.c:1-4','Current codec bridge qualifies codec names/configuration and uses maintained decoder/kernel stack. A progressive/precision/tool-specialized Wasm runtime is a distinct build/profile artifact; a source audit cannot infer startup benefit or safely drop uncommon tools.','Unexpected stream/config changes reject safely while admitted pictures remain exact under pinned compiler and codec settings.','Record one narrow progressive AVC tool set and current code-size/hot-path exposure; only then scope one specialized artifact with a changed-tool control.','Unsupported field/precision/tool input silently decoding differently rejects.','Total download/compile/startup/decode cost, not isolated instruction count.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','native/vd_browser.c:125-185;web/retained-engine-worker.js:18-38','Current frames are full AVFrame/VideoFrame surfaces and downstream draw expects them. Historical tiled sharing is postdecode after full comparisons, not decoder-internal COW. Tile table ownership plus flattening would be new representation work.','Immutable retained planar pictures reconstruct exactly and edits never mutate prior references, including filter-boundary consumers.','Profile one actual multi-frame retained owner, then compare postdecode tile sharing including equality scans and flattening before decoder changes.','A changed tile mutating an older frame or savings erased by flattening rejects.','Unique tile payload plus tables, scans, allocator overhead and presentation conversion.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','native/vd_browser.c:98-113;native/vd_browser.c:175-183','Current bridge retains recovery packets and waits for key entry after reset but has no per-picture contamination provenance graph. Historical exact output after next IDR supports conservative recovery, not certification inside arbitrary damaged GOPs.','Only independently certified unaffected output can be surfaced; unknown reference management remains untrusted until reset.','Define a source-generation trust flag for one lost nonreference picture and one reference loss before adding per-picture provenance.','Surfacing a dependent corrupted picture as exact or clearing trust before certified IDR rejects.','Useful trusted output retained without extra decode or hidden concealment claims.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','src/internal/playback-plans.ts:35-46;native/ao_browser.c:30-38','Effects are delegated to mpv; the app does not own fixed biquad block-state transforms or an edit timeline. Report double-precision model cannot serialize arbitrary Web Audio/mpv internal state, and no new effect subsystem is warranted in first pass.','Fixed linear recurrence, state coordinate system and exact/toleranced output contract include complete tails and source history.','Identify one controlled fixed biquad owner and compare one prefix transform-derived seek state against continuous replay before integration.','Coefficient automation, nonlinear stage or wrong initial state invalidates composed summaries.','Preparation plus state query work and residual replay, separately from waveform rendering.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','native/adaptation/flac.h:28-38;native/ao_browser.c:30-38','Local adaptation does not admit Vorbis decoding; software audio is continuous mpv-owned. Independent Vorbis jobs need packet/window overlap and global trimming before any parallel scheduler can safely splice PCM.','Complete continuous-reference PCM with correct window transition, global sample offsets and initial/end trim.','Inspect one pinned Vorbis packet stream and compare two jobs with a preceding packet, varying short/long window transition and EOF trim.','One-packet overlap failing a transition cannot be treated as universal closure.','Job setup, duplicated overlap, transfers and complete decode versus one continuous decoder.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','native/simd/h264-qpel.c:12-42;native/simd/h264-qpel.c:44-65','Actual qpel owner already reuses horizontal temporaries within a block. Historical H264-like cache is not a normative replacement across phases/chroma/weighted prediction; persistent cache needs finalized reference identity and measured hot repeat exposure.','Cache stage preserves exact unclipped intermediates and final pixels for the same reference/phase/geometry/numeric stage.','Instrument repeated nontrivial qpel keys in the pinned kernel before adding a bounded cache; compare an old/new reference at identical coordinates.','Reference identity omission or prematurely clipped intermediate rejects.','Actual repeat hit work versus hashing/storage/locality and cache memory.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','native/adaptation/flac.h:28-38;native/adaptation/flac.h:98-121;src/internal/playback-plans.ts:90-93','Current FLAC path requires established integer precision and rejects unqualified conversion. allowLossy applies Opus, not an explicit float quantization/error policy. Float-to-24-bit FLAC needs a separate requested fidelity contract; it must not weaken sample-exact admission.','Explicit permitted quantization reports RMS/peak error and clipping/headroom while preserving rate/layout and avoiding hidden dither/limiter choices.','Define a research-only float quantization contract on one in-range signal plus out-of-range rejection and compare against the same normal float decoder.','Calling FLAC roundtrip exact relative to original float or silently clipping rejects.','Full conversion/playback cost and error/size against integer-lossless and permitted lossy alternatives.')
row('DEFER_SETUP','src/internal/native-player.ts:320-336;native/adaptation/flac.h:28-38','Audio track switch currently restarts remux at the existing position; FLAC output preserves source rate/layout rather than enforcing a stable session configuration. A persistent audio producer and permitted common profile are needed, especially where native tracks differ.','Requested language/role remains selected, compatible rate/layout and exact integer samples preserved; heterogeneous conversion requires explicit permission.','Trace one pair of compatible integer tracks through current switch and measure interruption before designing one stable FLAC producer boundary.','Choosing wrong role, resampling without permission or claiming same decoder instance from same MIME rejects.','Switch gap/latency plus added conversion and retained-video ownership.')
row('ADVANCE_CONFIRMATION','src/internal/native-player.ts:36-51;src/internal/playback-plans.ts:35-46','Native already owns one media-element gain graph, providing a bounded insertion point for an explicitly requested channel-index matrix. Current admission does not support remapping, and historical six-channel index result does not justify semantic speaker guesses or downmix permission.','Declared known-layout matrix preserves intended channels/rate/headroom; identity must be transparent and any downmix remains explicitly requested.','In an isolated graph extension compare six-channel identity and one-index attenuation against OfflineAudioContext matrix reference, reusing the single media source.','Unknown speaker order, hidden mix, clipping or stale graph after source replacement rejects.','Added node/update/latency cost and verified per-channel matrix, not physical speaker routing.')
assert len(rows)==len(a)==56,(len(rows),len(a))
(p/'work/batch_f/audits').mkdir(exist_ok=True);out=[]
for item,(decision,owners,gap,contract,nxt,control,metric) in zip(a,rows):
 d=m.template(item);d.update(decision=decision,evidence_level='SOURCE_REVIEW',source_checked=True,hypothesis=item['source_excerpt'],tested_profile='Current-code first-pass applicability review for '+item['title']+'; historical source results are not rerun.',requested_output_contract=contract,current_code_paths=owners,observed_gap=gap,reason=gap,next_test=nxt,reopen_condition=nxt)
 d['baseline'].update(git_sha='c5a82ca0346d1e27be8f8007d4a68585ababcb75',plan='Read unchanged current owner against the precise proposal/report mechanism; preserve dirty checkout and maintain the scoped baseline identified in this audit.')
 d['probe'].update(method='Full definition and related report sections read; current owner inspected. No browser, component or benchmark execution.',positive_control='Proposed bounded follow-up: '+nxt,negative_control='Proposed falsifier: '+control,outcome=gap)
 d['measurement'].update(primary_metric=metric,worthwhile_change='Concrete capability or meaningful eliminated work in the stated workload after all listed preparation and ownership costs; no global percentage threshold.',result='No new measurement. Historical numeric results remain report claims with the stated scope.',uncertainty='Current-code applicability is not runtime correctness, physical energy, or qualification.',excluded_costs=['New execution was outside this source-review assignment.'])
 d['limits']=['No runtime test executed; read test code is not executed evidence.','Historical environment blocks are not automatically inherited; shared secure-origin prerequisites only establish APIs.','No source scripts executed, production changes, build, default-route promotion or qualification.']
 body='<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0 -->\n# '+item['key']+'\n\nDecision: '+decision+' / SOURCE_REVIEW\n\n## Full cited definition and report sections read\n'
 for s in [item['definition_source']]+item['related_reports']:
  raw=(p/s['path']).read_bytes();assert hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()==s['sha256'];lines=raw.decode().splitlines();body+=f"\n{s['path']}:{s['line_start']}-{s['line_end']} SHA256 {s['sha256']}\n\n"+'\n'.join(f'{i+1}: {lines[i]}' for i in range(s['line_start']-1,s['line_end']))+'\n'
 body+='\n## Current owner and applicability\n\n'+gap+'\n\n'
 for owner in owners:
  name=owner.split(':')[0];raw=pathlib.Path(name).read_bytes();body+='- '+owner+' SHA256 '+hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()+'\n'
 body+='\n## Hypothesis and contract\n\n'+d['hypothesis']+'\n\n'+contract+'\n\n## Baseline and decision\n\n'+d['baseline']['plan']+'\n\n'+gap+'\n\n## Metric and falsifier\n\n'+metric+'\n\n'+control+'\n\n## Next bounded test / reopen\n\n'+nxt+'\n\nNo new candidate executed or performance measured. This is a scoped first-pass decision, not a shippable feature or full qualification.\n'
 path=pathlib.Path('work/batch_f/audits')/(item['key']+'.md');(p/path).write_text(body);d['evidence']=[{'path':str(path),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(body.encode()).hexdigest(),'note':'Individual full-section source/current-owner audit, exact contract, scoped decision and falsifier.'}]
 if item['legacy_id'] in ['R359','R214','R083','R302']:
  q=p/'evidence/prerequisites/result.json';d['evidence'].append({'path':'evidence/prerequisites/result.json','sha256':hashlib.sha256(q.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'note':'Shared current secure-origin API prerequisite only; does not prove this mechanism or codec/configuration.'})
 m.validate_record(p,a,d);out.append(d)
(p/'work/batch_f/decisions.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2)+'\n')
from collections import Counter
print(Counter(d['decision'] for d in out));print(len(out),'drafts validated; ledger untouched')
